      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Yeah I agree here. in general, vrc seems to go out of their way to *hide* labs content. \nit's a shame you cant set labs worlds to home worlds. I imagine it's a by-product of labs worlds not technically being counted as public worlds. They are really only like semi-public.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-11-05T16:25:35.132Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I don't know if this is a bug, an oversight, or just the team being overly cautious, but currently if a world is going through Community Labs it cannot be set as a Home world.\nThis is not just an another unnecessary hurdle for Labs worlds but also goes against the principle of Labs: Assuming that popularity is the biggest factor in if a world passes Labs (which is how the system seems to work) then couldn't the number of people setting the world as Home be another indicator of its popularity?\nAs such, I think it only makes sense that we be allowed to set Labs worlds as a Home world.",
